<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    What Android may carry to a reinstall or a new phone. Devices on API 30 and
    below; API 31 and above read data_extraction_rules.xml instead.

    The database is deliberately included. It is the only copy of work that was done
    and money that was collected, and there is no pull sync yet — so if somebody
    reinstalls, this backup is the difference between their season being there and
    being gone. Auto Backup only ever restores onto a fresh install, never over a
    running one, so it cannot overwrite anything newer.

    The device identity is deliberately excluded. It is written into every job as
    lastWriterDeviceId and decides whose edit wins when the same job was changed on
    two phones; it has to be stable for one install and different between installs.
    Carrying it to a second phone would leave both of them claiming to be the same
    writer, and the merge would have no way to tell them apart. A fresh install
    generates a new one, which is the correct answer.
-->
<full-backup-content>
    <exclude domain="sharedpref" path="fieldtrack.device.xml"/>
    <!--
        Backup bookkeeping. "Last backed up at" describes what this install sent, and
        restoring it onto another phone would have that phone claim a backup it never
        made — the one thing the backup screen must never say.
    -->
    <exclude domain="sharedpref" path="fieldtrack.sync.xml"/>
</full-backup-content>
